= Recent trends <sec:trends>
\
\
Neurosymbolic RL looks different now than it did in the 2023 surveys @acharya2023 @yu2023. Five shifts stand out in work from 2023 to 2026. Some build on lines of research that go back before deep learning. Others are new and come from large language models showing up. @fig:timeline puts the systems this review talks about on a timeline.

